    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005809": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Associate",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26005809) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26005809) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005809 ) UPSOM Department of Medicine seeks an innovative, committed, and collaborative leader to serve as its inaugural Associate Dean for Assessment and Educational Evaluation. This is a pivotal moment in medical education, one defined by competency-based assessment, data-informed decision-making, and an unwavering commitment to continuous improvement. The Associate Dean will closely partner with the Assistant Dean for Accreditation and Continuous Quality Improvement (ACQI) in leading an office that spans assessment, evaluation (educational and non-educational), and ACQI. The Associate Dean will play a central role in shaping how UPSOM measures excellence, ensures accountability, and advances the quality and impact of its educational programs as it advances toward the goal of being recognized as one of the top 5 medical schools in the country. This position will be at the Associate Professor rank, appointment stream. Reporting to Abbas Hyderi, MD, MPH, Vice Dean for Education, the Associate Dean will design, implement, and oversee a comprehensive and integrated system of student assessment and educational program evaluation aligned with UPSOM’s mission, vision, and values. This leader will ensure that both learner performance and curricular effectiveness are systematically measured, thoughtfully analyzed, and continuously improved - building a culture where assessment is not episodic, but embedded, transparent, and mission-driven. In addition, the Associate Dean will lead efforts in curriculum mapping and integration to promote alignment of educational program objectives, course/clerkship objectives, and assessments. The role requires employing evidence-based approaches and contributing to national discussions on competency-based medical education, student assessment, educational program evaluation, and continuous improvement of medical education. The role will lead efforts in curriculum mapping and integration to enable the most effective alignment between instruction, learner assessment, and educational program evaluation. Primary Responsibilities: · Lead the design and implementation of a systematic program evaluation framework to monitor the effectiveness and quality of the curriculum and learning environment. · Analyze evaluation data and provide actionable recommendations for improvement to faculty, committees, and leadership. · Monitor evaluation outcomes, lead or guide associated quality improvement efforts as appropriate, and participate in the continuous quality improvement efforts. · Design, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive program of student assessment across the entirety of the curriculum, including working towards a competency-based medical approach. · Work with course and education program leaders to ensure a variety of robust student assessments (spanning medical knowledge, clinical skills, and workplace-based activities) that are aligned with UPSOM educational program objectives. · Work with course and education program leaders to ensure student assessments are aligned with accreditation expectations. Serve as content expert for LCME standards related to assessment. Prepare for and participate in accreditation reviews and site visits. Monitor and address any assessment or educational evaluation issues related to accreditation and regulatory compliance. · Monitor assessment outcomes, lead or guide associated continuous quality improvement efforts as appropriate and participate in the quality improvement efforts of the CQI Committee. · Create and oversee formative and summative assessment strategies, including performance-based assessments. · Employ evidence-based strategies and contribute to national discussions on competency-based medical education, student assessment, and continuous improvement of assessment initiatives. · Collaborate with information technology to streamline assessment and educational evaluation data collection, review, and monitoring including contributing to a nascent educational data warehouse. · Analyze and report data in a manner that effectively and clearly communicates student and program performance. · Lead data collection, processes, analyses, and reporting of student performance and post-graduation outcomes. · Prepare reports in support of accreditation and quality improvement processes. · Provide input into the Medical Student Performance Evaluation as needed. · Serve as a staff member on the Committee on Student Promotions to present select assessment information, answer questions, and provide context. · Oversee curriculum mapping to ensure alignment between educational program objectives, course/clerkship objectives, instructional methods, and assessment methods. · Collaborate with faculty and course leaders to identify gaps, redundancies, and opportunities for integration across the curriculum. · Ensure that curriculum maps are updated and maintained to support accreditation, student learning, and faculty development. · Work with the Curriculum Committee and related subcommittees to enhance horizontal and vertical integration of educational content and outcomes. · Provide direction and feedback to staff – support the hiring and onboarding of new staff. · Collaborate with school senior leadership to set and enforce overall assessment policies, procedures, and strategies. · Serve on internal and external committees related to role. · Disseminate experiences/scholarship in regional and national presentations and other activities to highlight the work done at UPSOM. · Build and maintain relationships with other medical schools, healthcare organizations, and community partners. · Serve as a member of the Vice Dean for Education leadership team. · Collaborate with and support the other assistant and associate deans with responsibilities in the medical education environment. Location: University of Pittsburgh is located in Pittsburgh, PA. Relocation to the Pittsburgh area is required for this role. Candidate Profile In terms of the performance and personal competencies required for the position, we would highlight the following: Education & Experience • A demonstrated leader in medical education (MD, PhD, EdD, or equivalent degree in a medical field) with an outstanding track record of accomplishment in medical education. • Five years of experience in undergraduate and/or graduate medical education with oversight of learner assessment and educational evaluation within a course, clerkship, or other curricular component. • 3-5 years of direct teaching experience of medical students, preferred. • Direct experience designing, implementing, and overseeing assessment systems and curricular program development. • Fundamental understanding of accreditation standards, regulatory expectations, and continuous quality improvement processes. • Experience contributing to accreditation preparation and review processes. • Deep expertise in program evaluation, learner assessment, data analysis, and quality improvement methodologies. • Evidence-informed approach to educational design and evaluation, with familiarity with the current literature and national landscape in competency-based medical education. • Track record of academic contributions that reflect intellectual rigor, creativity, and innovation in medical education. • Systems thinker with the ability to operate effectively across the medical school, university, and health system environments. • Forward-thinking in the use of technology, digital tools, and innovation in curricular design, assessment, and implementation. • Demonstrated ability to navigate complexity and ambiguity while translating strategy into effective execution. • Excellent communication and listening skills, with the ability to unite, inspire, and build consensus among students, faculty, staff, and institutional partners. • Mission-oriented and deeply committed to the future of medical education and to advancing student success and institutional excellence. • Collaborative relationship-building skills, with an ability to successfully partner and build consensus with key internal and external stakeholders at all levels of the organization and with external partners. Setting Strategy • The ability to create and articulate an inspiring vision for assessment and educational evaluation for the organization. • The inclination to seek and analyze data from a variety of sources to support assessment and educational evaluation decisions to align with the school’s strategic plan. • An entrepreneurial and creative approach to developing new, innovative ideas that will stretch the organization and push the boundaries within the industry. • The ability to effectively balance the desire/need for broad change with an understanding of how much change the organization is capable of handling, to create realistic goals and implementation plans that are achievable and successful. Executing for Results • The ability to set clear and challenging goals while committing the organization to improved performance; tenacious and accountable in driving results. • Comfortable with ambiguity and uncertainty; the ability to adapt nimbly and lead others through complex situations. • A risk-taker who seeks data and input from others to foresee possible threats or unintended circumstances from decisions; someone who takes smart risks. • A leader who is viewed by others as having a high degree of integrity and forethought in their approach to making decisions; the ability to act in a transparent and consistent manner while always taking into account what is best for the organization. Leading Teams • A leader who is self-reflective and aware of their own limitations; leads by example and drives the organization's performance with an attitude of continuous improvement by being open to feedback and self-improvement. • Naturally connects and builds strong and authentic relationships with others, demonstrating strong emotional intelligence and an ability to communicate clearly and persuasively. • The ability to persevere in the face of challenges, and exhibit a steadfast resolve and relentless commitment to higher standards, which elicits respect from followers. Nomination and Application Procedure To receive full consideration, interested individuals should electronically submit a Curriculum Vitae and a letter of interest to requisition number 26005809 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The letter of interest is a two to three-page cover letter detailing your experience and key achievements related to this position and your thoughts on how you see yourself contributing to the programs and responsibilities described in this position specification. Letters should be addressed to the University of Pittsburgh Associate Dean for Assessment and Educational Evaluation Search Committee and submitted electronically. Materials will be reviewed immediately and will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005525": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005525) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005525) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Dent Med-Periodontics/Preventive Dentistry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005525 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine, with its Dental Hygiene Program in the Department of Periodontics and Preventive Dentistry, announces the immediate availability of one full-time (12-month) non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Rank and salary are commensurate with education, teaching, and professional experience.  Candidates must be a graduate of a CODA-accredited dental hygiene program and have at least 5 years of clinical or professional experience; a master's degree or higher in a related field and at least 3 years teaching experience are preferred.  Candidates must also possess or be eligible for Pennsylvania dental hygiene licensure and a local anesthesia permit, and a background check is required prior to the official offer. Primary responsibilities include clinical, laboratory, and didactic instruction for the Dental Hygiene Associate Degree program, with additional duties that include committee work, student advising, scholarly activities, research, professional organization participation, community service, and faculty practice. Pitt Dental Medicine is located on the University main campus in Pittsburgh, contiguous with the other five health science schools. The school's general dental clinics and 11 specialty clinics play an integral role in improving the oral health of the patient population of southwestern Pennsylvania and beyond. As part of the clinical practice and faculty of the University of Pittsburgh, the practitioner will have the opportunity to collaborate with clinicians, innovators, and investigators from around the world and become part of a vibrant community of healthcare providers dedicated to making a difference in their chosen field and in the lives of others. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a CV, and three letters of recommendation. Salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. To apply, please go to join.pitt.edu, select Faculty Positions, and enter 26005525 in the keyword search. Please upload a curriculum vitae and a statement describing your interest in the position, qualifications, and experience. The search committee will begin reviewing applications upon receipt. Only applicants who appear best qualified will be invited for a personal interview. The candidate must provide at least three letters of recommendation. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005411": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Associate",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Part-Time (26005411) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Part-Time (26005411) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Associate - Part-Time Med-Ophthalmology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005411 ) University of Pittsburgh, Ophthalmology Department is searching for a Part-time, Associate Professor, Appointment-stream position. We expect the position to develop Clinical trial and Biostatistical design and participate in Disease monitoring and review. Position may also participate in the mentor of postdoctoral fellows and graduate students, submit grants, prepare manuscripts and publications, make research presentations, and participate in the activities of the local, national, and international neuroscience and ophthalmology communities. Minimum experience: 10+ years of Biostatistical/Bioinformatics Health or Research experience PhD in Biostatistics required Please apply through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center using this link Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh.  Under Requisition #: 26005411 The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005438": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005438) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005438) Job Description Faculty Professor - Full-Time Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005438 ) Qualified applicants seeking opportunities in clinical programs may find recruitment in The Department of Pediatrics of the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine Pediatric subspecialty programs: Our Subspecialties include: • Adolescent Medicine • Allergy • Bone Marrow Transplantation • Cardiology • Child Advocacy • Child Development • Hospitalists • Emergency Medicine • Endocrinology • Gastroenterology • General Academic Pediatrics • Hematology/Oncology • Infectious Diseases • Newborn Medicine • Neurology • Palliative Care and Supportive Medicine • Pulmonology • Rheumatology Job Description and Qualifications The position is for the recruitment of an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the appointment (non-tenure) stream. Available positions are open to all applicants who hold a doctoral-level degree Education in the field of medicine (MD, DO), are board certified or board eligible, are qualified for medical licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, and meet the minimum position credentials for the pediatric specialty to provide clinical service. Responsibilities will include patient care, teaching, and research as determined by the chairman and the associated division chief. Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor positions in the appointment stream at the University of Pittsburgh, with rank and salary commensurate with experience and academic credentials. General rank requirements: Assistant Professors have 1-6 years of experience with demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Associate Professors have 7-10 years of experience with significant demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Professors have 10 or more years of experience with a clear demonstration of leadership, academic excellence and innovation in their pediatric specialty. Not all divisions have active recruitments; however, interested candidates can inquire about potential opportunities available in the Department of Pediatrics by applying to requisition number # 26005438 on Pitt Talent Center by visiting https://www.join.pitt.edu/ The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. See appended Job Posting The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004200": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time (26004200) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time (26004200) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time Med-Psychiatry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004200 ) Research Assistant Professor of Psychiatry University of Pittsburgh, Department of Psychiatry Pittsburgh, United States Job description The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking a full-time Research Assistant Professor i n the appointment stream to contribute to and advance research in psychiatric illness and mental health. The incumbent’s responsibilities will include: · Conducting independent and collaborative research focused on the neurobiological substrates of complex human cognitive functions, and how alterations in these systems contribute to cognitive dysfunction. · Contributing to the design, execution, and dissemination of research studies, including assisting in the preparation of manuscripts and participation in grant writing. · Supporting and, where appropriate, overseeing aspects of lab operations, including project coordination and mentorship of trainees or junior staff. · Ensuring all research activities are conducted in accordance with university, federal, and other applicable guidelines governing the responsible conduct of research. The search committee will primarily be looking for demonstrated experience in: · Contributing to collaborative neuroscience or related research, with increasing independence. · Implementing research studies and contributing to publications. · Providing training and mentorship in research methods and laboratory procedures. Successful candidates will join a vibrant and highly interactive research community with a long history of excellence in basic and translational neuroscience research. Qualifications: · PhD in Neuroscience, Psychology, or a related field. · Demonstrated interest in psychiatry research (e.g., through poster presentations). · Demonstrated research skills, with an emerging record of independence. · Strong organizational and project management skills. · Ability to work effectively in a dynamic and growing academic environment. About the Employer At the University of Pittsburgh Department of Psychiatry, we excel in our mission to: Provide superb behavioral health services to our patients and their families; Pursue the development of improved diagnostic techniques and therapeutic interventions through innovative research; Provide a stimulating learning environment for medical and graduate students, residents, psychology interns, and postdoctoral fellows. Our success in each of these areas depends on a highly interactive community of clinicians, scientists, and educators who bring diversity in background, experience, expertise, and perspective to our mission. An essential partner in this work is UPMC Western Psychiatric Hospital, a national leader in innovative treatment of mental health and addiction disorders. Pitt Psychiatry’s faculty of more than 230 members across basic and clinical science disciplines is central to our success in advancing research, education, and clinical care. Areas of Research Psychology Psychiatry Neuroscience How to Apply Please apply by going to our job site ( https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobsearch.ftl ), searching job code 26004200 in the keyword search, and submitting your materials through our Pitt system. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005436": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005436) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005436) Job Description Faculty Professor - Full-Time Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005436 ) Qualified applicants seeking opportunities in clinical programs may find recruitment in The Department of Pediatrics of the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine Pediatric subspecialty programs: Our Subspecialties include: • Adolescent Medicine • Allergy • Bone Marrow Transplantation • Cardiology • Child Advocacy • Child Development • Hospitalists • Emergency Medicine • Endocrinology • Gastroenterology • General Academic Pediatrics • Hematology/Oncology • Infectious Diseases • Newborn Medicine • Neurology • Palliative Care and Supportive Medicine • Pulmonology • Rheumatology Job Description and Qualifications The position is for the recruitment of an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the appointment (non-tenure) stream. Available positions are open to all applicants who hold a doctoral-level degree Education in the field of medicine (MD, DO), are board certified or board eligible, are qualified for medical licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, and meet the minimum position credentials for the pediatric specialty to provide clinical service. Responsibilities will include patient care, teaching, and research as determined by the chairman and the associated division chief. Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor positions in the appointment stream at the University of Pittsburgh, with rank and salary commensurate with experience and academic credentials. General rank requirements: Assistant Professors have 1-6 years of experience with demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Associate Professors have 7-10 years of experience with significant demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Professors have 10 or more years of experience with a clear demonstration of leadership, academic excellence and innovation in their pediatric specialty. Not all divisions have active recruitments; however, interested candidates can inquire about potential opportunities available in the Department of Pediatrics by applying to requisition number # 26005436 on Pitt Talent Center by visiting https://www.join.pitt.edu/ The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. See appended Job Posting The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005544": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005544) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005544) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Emergency Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005544 ) The University of Pittsburgh Physicians (UPP) Emergency Medicine is recruiting a physician to join our expanding team. The successful candidate will practice as a physician in a dual capacity within the UPP Emergency Medicine and the University of Pittsburgh Department of Emergency Medicine to include clinical, research and/or teaching responsibilities. For example: • Contribute to teaching, mentoring, and service activities consistent with rank and departmental needs. • Collaborate with departmental and interdisciplinary research teams at Pitt and UPMC. • Publish scholarly work in peer-reviewed journals and present findings at professional/scientific meetings. He/she will participate in outreach efforts for the Emergency Department, expanding inpatient and outpatient activities at locations within the Emergency Medicine service area. As a faculty member, the successful candidate will actively participate in the research and educational mission of the Emergency Medicine Department. Emergency Medicine is looking to hire a faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the appointment stream. The candidate should have demonstrated teaching ability, experience in advanced study and research, or professional experience of a kind which would enable him or her to make a comparable academic contribution. He or she should exhibit promise of originality and excellence in some field connected with teaching, writing, or research, and should have demonstrated ability in guiding and counseling students. Available positions are open to all applicants who hold doctoral level education in the field of emergency medicine (MD, DO), are ABEM/ABOEM board certified or eligible, are qualified for medical licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, and completed necessary training in Emergency Medicine. General rank requirements: An assistant professor should have demonstrated teaching ability, experience in advanced study and research, or professional experience of a kind which would enable them to make an academic contribution. Interested candidates should apply via Pitt Talent Center at join.pitt.edu with REQUISITION NUMBER 26005544. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. n/a The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005395": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005395) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005395) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Psychiatry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005395 ) Assistant Professor of Psychiatry University of Pittsburgh, Department of Psychiatry Pittsburgh, United States Job Description The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking researchers for full-time faculty positions investigating psychiatric illness. Positions are available at the assistant professor level within the appointment (non-tenure) stream. Growth is sought in both preclinical and clinical approaches towards understanding psychiatric illness. Consequently, multiple positions are available. Primary selection criteria are history of productivity and ability to enhance an interactive and dynamic mental health research community within and across departments in the greater Pittsburgh academic environment. Primarily, the search committee will look for: Success in authoring papers published in refereed journals. These may include original research and review articles. The quality of the journals themselves and the position of authorship will also be considered. Success in securing federal funding from the National Institutes of Health (NIH). However, success in obtaining funding from other sources (such as state and foundation funding) will also be considered. Presentations of research and/or scholarly material and published abstracts associated with professional or scientific meetings. Successful candidates will join a vibrant and highly interactive research community with a long history of excellence in basic, translational, and clinical research. The Department of Psychiatry is prepared to invest substantial resources to ensure success. Qualifications: PhD in Psychology, Neuroscience, Translational Science, or related field. Demonstrated research skills Strong organizational skills Flexibility and ability to work in a rapidly changing/growing educational institution Job Responsibilities: · Establish and sustain an independent, externally funded research program in psychiatric illness · Publish scholarly work in peer ‑ reviewed journals and present findings at professional meetings. · Collaborate with departmental and interdisciplinary research teams at Pitt and UPMC. · Contribute to the academic mission through teaching, mentoring, and service, as appropriate. About the Employer At the University of Pittsburgh Department of Psychiatry, we excel in our mission to: provide superb behavioral health services to our patients and their families; pursue the development of better diagnostic techniques and therapeutic interventions through innovative research; provide a stimulating learning environment for medical and graduate students, residents, psychology interns, and postdoctoral fellows. An essential partner in this work is UPMC Western Psychiatric Hospital, a national leader in innovative treatment of mental health and addiction disorders. Moreover, Pitt Psychiatry's preeminent academic faculty of more than 230 members trained in multiple basic and clinical science disciplines is at the heart of our success in providing superior behavioral health care and in training the next generation of innovative researchers and clinicians. Areas of Research Psychology Psychiatry Neuroscience How to Apply Please apply by going to our job site ( https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobsearch.ftl ), searching job code 26005395 in the keyword search, and submitting your materials through our Pitt system. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005459": {
